  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Boosting Youth Employment in the South of Libya, Through Skills Enhancement and Livelihood Opportunities</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project has been developed based on the interest of proposing a sustainable local development project to be implemented by ENA, which aims at responding to local needs while targeting the most vulnerable Libyans. Through this 48-months project in partnership with IOM, the wider efforts done in Sabha and the south of Libya on livelihoods promotion and social cohesion, that have been at the core of IOM&#x2019;s work in the south since 2016, will be maximised. Moreover, the project will build upon IOM&#x2019;s previous work conducted on TVET curricula development and infrastructure rehabilitation to strengthen learning and job pathways for youth from different regions in the south of Libya through curricula development tailored to the Fezzan market needs, rehabilitation of a TVET centre already identified in Sabha by the MOL and through private sector and agricultural cooperatives/associations engagement.</narrative>
  </description>
